# §16.13 c5 — keep the docker build context lean + secret-free.
#
# Docker sends the entire context tarball to the daemon before
# building. Without this file, that includes .venv (hundreds of MB),
# node_modules (similar), every committed-test artifact, the dev
# SQLite DB (potentially containing imported library metadata), and
# the .git history. All slow, none useful.
#
# What we DO want sent: the source the Dockerfile's COPY lines pull
# from — pyproject, the Python packages, stations/, migrations/,
# alembic.ini, README, LICENSE, and `web/` (sans node_modules and
# build artifacts — npm ci rebuilds them inside the build stage).

# ---- dev environments (huge, not source of truth) ----
.venv/
**/__pycache__/
*.pyc
*.pyo
.pytest_cache/
.coverage
.coverage.*
htmlcov/

# ---- node-side dev artifacts ----
# web/node_modules — rebuilt fresh in stage 1 from package-lock.json.
# web/build      — rebuilt fresh in stage 1 from web/src/.
# web/.svelte-kit — SvelteKit cache, not needed.
node_modules/
web/node_modules/
web/build/
web/.svelte-kit/

# ---- secrets + local state (NEVER ship to a build context) ----
# Working SQLite DBs accumulate as the dev clicks around. They may
# contain personal iTunes-library metadata. Hard-exclude.
*.db
*.db-wal
*.db-shm
*.sqlite
*.sqlite3
.env
.env.*
station_studio.db
tmp_check.db

# ---- test detritus ----
# c5-review 🟡-3: exclude the whole `tests/` tree from the build
# context, not just its __pycache__. The Dockerfile doesn't COPY
# tests/, so shipping ~MB of pytest source + fixtures to the daemon
# on every build is pure waste. Same for web/e2e (Playwright specs).
tests/
web/e2e/
playwright-test*
playwright-test.*.db
playwright-test.*.db-wal
playwright-test.*.db-shm
playwright-report/
web/test-results/
web/playwright-report/
test-results/

# ---- build outputs (rebuilt inside the image) ----
dist/
build/
*.egg-info/
*.whl
*.tar.gz

# ---- editor + OS noise ----
.DS_Store
.vscode/
.idea/
*.swp

# ---- VCS (we don't need git history at build time) ----
.git/
.gitignore

# ---- runtime output dirs (per-dev, never bundled) ----
output/
from_user/
backups/
out/

# ---- docs that don't affect the build ----
# DESIGN.md is large but the Dockerfile does COPY README.md + LICENSE
# explicitly; DESIGN/CONTRIBUTING don't need to be in the context.
DESIGN.md
CONTRIBUTING.md
docs/
